## Skill precedence

The saga plugin provides four skills with generic best-practice defaults:
`spring-boot-patterns`, `jooq-conventions`, `postgres-migrations`, `testcontainers-testing`.

Each skill's `## Codebase conventions` section instructs Claude to load a
project-specific override file from `.claude/context/conventions/<skill-name>.md`.
**When that file exists, it wins — it takes precedence over everything in the
plugin's skill file.** Generic skill guidance only applies when no override file
is present for that skill.

If you see Claude follow the generic skill pattern instead of a project-specific
one, check that `/init-context` has been run and that the relevant file exists
under `.claude/context/conventions/`.

## Workflow

1. `/design <spec.md>` — produces a design doc, stops for human review
2. `/approve-design` — human gate, unlocks implementation
3. `/implement` — implements the approved design with tests
4. `/mark-reviewed` — human gate, unlocks finishing
5. `/finish` — changelog entry, commit, optional push/PR

Writes to source files are blocked by a hook until the design for the current
workflow state is approved; commits/pushes are blocked until code review is
marked complete. See `hooks/hooks.json` in the plugin if you need to debug why
something was blocked.
